1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 d6 4. d4 a6 5. Bxc6+ bxc6 6. dxe5 Bg4 7. O-O Bxf3 8. Qxf3 dxe5 9. Qc3 Qd6 10. Nd2 Qc5 11. Nc4 Bd6 12. Be3 Qb5 13. a4 Qb7 14. Nxe5 Ne7 15. Nc4 f6 16. e5 Bb4 17. Qb3 Nd5 18. c3 Nxe3 19. fxe3 Rb8 20. cxb4 Qxb4 21. Nd6+ {Sources: CHESS, December 1942, Vol.8/87; Belfast News-Letter, 9 December 1942; Ilford Recorder, 14 January 1943. Both 'Chess' and the British Chess Magazine list the players as being placed on board 11, though the Hastings and St Leonards Observer of 14.11.1942 states that the game was played on board 12. The Black player is given as T G Bot in the Hastings and St Leonards Observer of the above date and the British Chess Magazine. His initials are also given as T.G. in the match score for CHESS, December 1942, Vol.8/87, though for the game itself he is listed as J C Bot in that magazine. The Ilford Recorder columnist acknowledged that he had taken the game from CHESS. He stated that the game was played on board 11 but gives Bot's initials as J.C. The Belfast News-Letter version does not give Bot's initials. (Denman Collection)} 1-0

